From d9108bfdb746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shivam Rawat <shivrawa@qti.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend

The Linux 7.2 implementation clears GMU_STATUS_FW_START and returns from
a6xx_rpmh_stop(), which skips the GPU RSCC power-off sequence and leaves
stale BCM votes.  This is the upstream fix carried by Linux 7.3 and stable
updates: run the stop sequence when firmware was started, and hold the GMU
CM3 in reset before asking RSCC to power down.

Upstream commit: d9108bfdb746
Fixes: f248d5d5159a ("drm/msm/a6xx: Fix PDC sleep sequence")
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@ static void a6xx_rpmh_stop(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
@@ -1465,6 +1465,9 @@ static void a6xx_gmu_shutdown(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	/* Stop the interrupts and mask the hardware */
 	a6xx_gmu_irq_disable(gmu);
 
+	/* Halt the gmu cm3 core */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 1);
+
 	/* Tell RPMh to power off the GPU */
 	a6xx_rpmh_stop(gmu);
 
